<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<h1>Todger <small>&amp; the</small> Ghoulies</h1>
<p>Britain's most-gripped rock band. Hard, loud and over far too soon.</p>
<span class="sticker">Now touring. Bring a towel.</span>
</div></header>

<main>
<section class="story"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Our Story (It's a Long One)</h2>
<p class="sub">Don't worry, we always give it a good go.</p>
<p>It all began in a damp rehearsal garage, where five very different men (and one spiritual presence) discovered they shared a single passion: making a lot of noise in confined spaces. Todger & the Ghoulies were formed after a heated argument over who had the biggest amp. Nobody won. Everybody measured.</p>
<p>Since then the band has gone from strength to strength, and occasionally to Scunthorpe. Critics describe the live show as "firm", "raw", and "a lot to take in". Fans are advised to arrive early, bring protection (earplugs) and be prepared to finish with a sore throat.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="alt"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Meet the Ghoulies</h2>
<p class="sub">Five members. Two guitars. One bassoon. Zero shame.</p>
<div class="grid">

<article class="card"><div class="badge">V</div>
<h3>Vladyslav</h3><p class="role">Lead guitar, solos of "considerable length"</p>
<p>Born in a Carpathian village where he found his first guitar in a haystack (the needle was nowhere to be seen). Vladyslav learned to shred at six, and has been working on his fingering ever since. His solos are famously long. Audiences regularly report that they "didn't think it would ever end", and then, once it did, that they "needed a minute".</p>
<p class="stats">Known for: a very firm grip on the neck. Weakness: a premature fade-out when the crowd gets too excited.</p></article>

<article class="card"><div class="badge">R</div>
<h3>Robbie Michael Freeman</h3><p class="role">Drums &amp; bassoon, a man of two hard shafts</p>
<p>Robbie was thrown out of the Neath Youth Orchestra for "unreasonable use of the double reed", and has been hitting things hard ever since. He is the only drummer in rock who also blows a bassoon on stage, which he describes as "keeping both ends busy". His sticks are always out and his rolls are legendary.</p>
<p class="stats">Known for: pounding. Always carries a spare pair of sticks, because he goes through them fast.</p></article>

<article class="card"><div class="badge">T</div>
<h3>Tyler Arthur Michael Morgan</h3><p class="role">Lead vocals, three names, one huge range</p>
<p>A former choirboy whose voice dropped at fourteen and, according to his mother, never properly came back up. Tyler gargles raw eggs before every gig and can hit notes so high the neighbours complain. He needs all three first names because "it takes that long to warm up". Frequently seen with a microphone in his hand and a lump in his throat.</p>
<p class="stats">Known for: swallowing the whole mic. Warning: may leave the stage glistening.</p></article>

<article class="card"><div class="badge">M</div>
<h3>Matty von Flue</h3><p class="role">Rhythm guitar, steady as she goes</p>
<p>Descended from a noble Swiss line of chimney sweeps, Matty's family has been going in and out of tight, dark spaces for centuries. He took up rhythm guitar because "someone has to keep a steady pace while Vladyslav goes on and on". Never rushes, never finishes early, and always makes sure everyone is warmed up and well lubricated (the strings, obviously).</p>
<p class="stats">Known for: staying hard all night. His family motto: "We always clean up after."</p></article>

<article class="card ghost"><div class="badge">?</div>
<h3>Rowan "Low End" Deepwell</h3><p class="role">Bass guitar. Does not exist.</p>
<p>The band's bassist is a deep, mysterious presence who has been spotted lurking at the back of gigs, handling the heavy low end. Rowan does not appear on any payroll, passport or group chat, and has therefore never once complained about the van. Described by those who have not met them as "tall, short, or possibly both". Gender: currently pending. They go deep, they stay low, and they are never available when the band needs a lift.</p>
<p class="stats">Pronouns: they/them/TBC. Status: legally fictional but emotionally committed.</p></article>

</div></div></section>

